    "updated_at": "2015-09-16T19:24:37Z",
    "body": "(Review continues...)\n\nI think you should probably open a new issue for yourself to uniformize all byte sequences in the spec to use backticks. It will be a big improvement in e.g. https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#prescan-a-byte-stream-to-determine-its-encoding\n\n> Let this instance of the fetching algorithm be associated with image request.\n\nThis is pretty weird. I can't find where it is needed either.\n\n> The resource obtained in this fashion, if any, is image request's image data.\n\nShouldn't this be using the response concept?\n\n>  Let client be img element's node document's\n\nMissing \"the\" before img.\n\n> Set request's client to client, type to \"image\", and set request's synchronous flag.\n\nHmm I don't see synchronous behavior in the original. Is this really correct? Doesn't it jank pages? Same for workers. I'm probably just missing something that makes it OK....\n\nThe sentence \"User agents should ignore HTTP cache headers in the response, never caching event sources.\" got lost. Was that on purpose?\n\n> Let request be request.\n\nI know I've seen this kind of thing in specs before but I think it's much clearer to say e.g. \"Let request be the EventSource object's request\"\n\n> process the response obtained in this fashion, if any, as described earlier in this section.\n\nI think the clarity here could be greatly improved, although I admit I am asking for changes to problems that were already there. I'd suggest labeling the section starting with \"As data is received, the tasks queued by the networking task source to handle the data must act as follows.\" with some heading or `<dfn>`, like \"process an EventSource response\". Then you can link to it instead of saying \"see a few paragraphs up somewhere\". It would also be ideal to move it to be a sibling of \"Parsing an event stream\".\n\n> e.g., the server returned a 4xx or 5xx status, or there was a DNS error\n\nCan probably make this more precise by using network error and ok status, right?\n\n---\n\nReview finished!!\n",
