    "body": "@domenic \n\n> Hmm I don't see synchronous behavior in the original. Is this really correct? Doesn't it jank pages? Same for workers. I'm probably just missing something that makes it OK....\n\nThe steps in which the fetch happens is \"in parallel\" in img-environment-changes algo, and the worker fetch happens in the worker's context, so they should be sync. The fetch in \"update the image data\" could also be made sync if we end the \"synchronous section\" before starting the fetch, but it doesn't need to be in this PR.\n",
